---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { contact, site } from '../site'
---
<Legal title="Terms & Conditions" description={`The terms that apply when you use ${site.name}.`}>
  <p>These terms apply when you use {site.name} at <a href={site.appUrl}>{site.appUrl}</a>, operated by {site.owner} ("we"). By using {site.name} you agree to them.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>You sign in with a GitHub or Google account and are responsible for activity under it. Keep that account secure and tell us if you think it has been misused.</p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not use {site.name} to break the law, infringe others' rights, send spam, upload malware, or try to disrupt or gain unauthorised access to the service or other users' data.</p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>You keep ownership of what you create in {site.name}. You give us permission to store and process it only as needed to run the app for you.</p>

  <h2>Paid access</h2>
  <p>Some features may require a paid subscription. Any price and billing terms are shown before you subscribe, and you can cancel at any time; access continues until the end of the paid period.</p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>We work to keep {site.name} available and useful, but we may change, suspend or discontinue features. We will give reasonable notice of changes that significantly affect you.</p>

  <h2>Disclaimer and liability</h2>
  <p>{site.name} is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for loss of data, arising from your use of the app.</p>

  <h2>Ending your use</h2>
  <p>You can stop using {site.name} and ask us to delete your account at any time. We may suspend accounts that break these terms.</p>

  {site.governingLaw && (
    <>
      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of {site.governingLaw}.</p>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? You can {contact}.</p>
</Legal>
